    "converged_on_repeaters_only": 0,
    "finding": "BG/NBD does not converge by maximum likelihood on this base — at any time scale tried (days, weeks, months), at any penalty from 0 to 10, on the full base or on the repeaters alone. The likelihood returns NaN and the parameters run off in log space. This is not a library defect or a tuning problem: BG/NBD's dropout parameters describe the shape of a Beta distribution over the probability of churning after each purchase, and they are identified only by the pattern of repeat purchasing. Olist's repeaters average 1.11 repeat purchases each, so there is nothing for those parameters to be estimated from and the likelihood is flat in them."
